bolo's own source code contains no third-party source code. It talks to the
following components, which are installed separately as Python dependencies
or optional extras and keep their own licences:

  Runtime dependencies
    FastAPI (MIT), Starlette (BSD-3-Clause), Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause),
    python-multipart (Apache-2.0), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), httpx (BSD-3-Clause),
    PyYAML (MIT), psutil (BSD-3-Clause),
    soundfile (BSD-3-Clause; its wheels bundle libsndfile, LGPL-2.1-or-later,
      with libFLAC, libogg, libvorbis, libopus (BSD-style), mpg123 (LGPL-2.1)
      and LAME (LGPL-2.0-or-later)),
    soxr (the Python binding and libsoxr are LGPL-2.1-or-later).

  Optional inference engines
    sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0)        https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
    ONNX Runtime (MIT), bundled in the sherpa-onnx wheel
    faster-whisper (MIT)            https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper
    CTranslate2 (MIT)               https://github.com/OpenNMT/CTranslate2
    useful-moonshine-onnx (MIT), pywhispercpp / whisper.cpp (MIT)
    kokoro-onnx (MIT; depends on phonemizer, GPL-3.0-or-later; not part of
      the "all" extra)

  Optional protocol and codec libraries
    wyoming (MIT)                   https://github.com/OHF-Voice/wyoming
    PyAV (BSD-3-Clause; its wheels bundle FFmpeg libraries, LGPL-2.1-or-later)

  Speaker diarization uses the pyannote segmentation-3.0 model (MIT) in its
  ONNX export and a 3D-Speaker ERes2Net speaker-embedding model (Apache-2.0),
  both run by sherpa-onnx. Model files are downloaded by the user, not
  distributed with bolo.

  eSpeak NG (GPL-3.0-or-later, https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng) is an
  OPTIONAL component. It is NOT bundled with bolo, not linked into it, not a
  dependency of the "all" extra and not in the default container images. It
  is installed only when the operator asks for it (the console, "bolo
  components install espeak-ng", the "espeak" extra, which pulls the
  third-party espeakng-loader wheel, or the system package manager) and
  after accepting its licence. Piper-format voices, KittenTTS, Matcha-TTS
  (English) and the non-English Kokoro voices need it; the default voice
  (Kokoro, English) does not. See docs/models.md, "Licences and the
  espeak-ng question".

API compatibility
    The routes under "speaches-compatible" mirror the HTTP interface of
    speaches (https://github.com/speaches-ai/speaches, MIT licence,
    Copyright (c) 2024 Fedir Zadniprovskyi) so that its clients keep
    working. The interface was re-implemented from its route definitions;
    no speaches source code is included.

Models
    Models are not distributed with bolo. They are downloaded on request
    from their publishers, under the licences recorded for each entry in
    the catalog (server/src/bolo/catalog/*.yaml).

Built-in audio samples
    The files in server/src/bolo/samples/*.wav were synthesised with bolo
    using the models named in server/src/bolo/samples/index.json.
